  "body": "What happens: `posting::default_machine()` (`crates/app/src/posting.rs:170-183`) logs the error and returns `Value::Null` when the default machine file is missing or malformed. The comment at `posting.rs:173-174` says \"the null machine refuses the post downstream\". No such refusal exists.\n\n- `engine::run` reads `Value::Null` as \"no machine\" (`crates/post/src/post/engine.rs:60-63`).\n- `machine::script_props` (`crates/post/src/post/machine.rs:211-232`) then sets rapid, feed and spindle limits to 0.0 and the coolant list to empty.\n- `posting_mounts.rs:68` uses `default_machine()` when the document has no machine.\n\nResult: the post writes a program with default machine values. It does not refuse. The program can have no coolant word and no machine limits.\n\nExpected: the post is refused with a message that names the missing or malformed machine file (Prime Directive: correct output or a visible refusal).\n\nEvidence: found by code reading in the review of PR #2318 (see the review comment there, and the comment on issue #2316). The exact output text was not recorded. The case occurs only when the default machine file is absent and the posts folder is present.\n\nDone means:\n- A post with a null machine is refused, with the file named in the message.\n- A test pins the refusal for a missing file and for a malformed file.\n- The comment at `posting.rs:173-174` is true.\n",
